BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.8 Tm /F3 10 Tf 14.2 TL .925 Tw (The digest is signed with an Ed25519 keypair over a fixed message format. Ed25519 is used for three reasons: it is) Tj T* 0 Tw .502778 Tw (deterministic, so signing the same message twice yields identical bytes and there is no nonce-reuse failure mode; it is) Tj T* 0 Tw .7305 Tw (fast enough that verification is trivial in a browser; and it is the native signature scheme of Solana, which means the) Tj T* 0 Tw (same key material serves both the attestation and the anchoring step without a second key hierarchy.) Tj T* ET
